well it is no secret that lake mead is  slowly running out of water but what we  haven't heard about is lake las vegas  it's about 30 minute drive from the  strip it's used for recreation and the  site where a lot of luxury homes are  being built the 8 news now i-team has  been learning the lake is currently not  getting filled the i-team's vanessa  murphy has the details from lake las  vegas again located in henderson  aside from the occasional raindrops like  we're seeing today we've learned lake  las vegas is currently getting no new  water that's because lake mead is so low  and this happened sooner than expected  the water for lake las vegas was coming  from basic water company also known as  basic management inc through the city of  henderson as the eight news now i-team  first reported in may basics intake pipe  gathered water at 1050  feet the lake level is now 1040 feet  according to a city of henderson  spokesperson basics intake ceased  operations on july first lake las vegas  was aware of this issue and put  additional water in the lake before that  a city of henderson spokesperson says  lake las vegas and the city are  currently working on a long-term  solution i spoke with a developer for  lake las vegas he says he expects this  to be totally sorted out within two to  three weeks he says the situation with  basics intake pipe happened about two  months sooner than expected but he  insists there's no problem here he says  infrastructure has been put in place to  address the issue and he says it's just  paperwork that needs to be finalized  now the lake needs to be supplied with  water because it evaporates the city of  henderson reports delivering 1.3 billion  gallons of water to the lake from july  to june of 2021 that increased to 1.5  billion this year again because lake las  vegas put extra water in the lake to  make up for the change since lake mead  is so low  now if you've been to lake las vegas you  know there are restaurants here there  are water sports over here you can see  there's some construction again the  developer insists none of this will be  affected reporting at lake las vegas  vanessa murphy live local now
 

